    "statement": "iPhone 14 Pro / Pro Max no touch with normal connector readings is usually a faulty touch boost capacitor C9201, which must be replaced.",
    "evidence": "Solution.",
    "quote": "",
    "at": ""
   },
   {
    "statement": "To check the boost, power the board at 3.8–4.2 V, inject 1.8 V into enable pin #31 (JC Drawing) and measure output pin #44; replace U9200 if the short persists.",
    "evidence": "Diagnostic and repair steps.",
    "quote": "",
    "at": ""
   }
  ],
